      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`LayerWiseLoadCounter.finish()` can return `False` and remove its batch as soon as the first failed Future is observed, even when a later layer is unresolved. Its documented wait-for-every-layer barrier should also hold on the failure path.\n\nFixes https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45467.\n\n## Modifications\n\nResolve each Future before aggregating success, preserving failure reporting after the forward and retaining the batch until all layer completions are observed. Extend the existing waiting test with success/failed-first-layer cases; always resolve its pending Future in `finally` so a failed assertion cannot strand the worker.\n\nThis is completion-counter semantics hardening. The regression constructs a failed-first/pending-later Future state directly; it does not reproduce active GPU/RDMA writes or prove physical transfer termination. No engine, transport or page-allocation lifecycle is added.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n`python -m pytest -q test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_unified_cache_linker.py -k layer_counter`\n\n- Main `533020b500ba781bfafd1f5cbadabaf03d8986f7` with the regression: **1 failed, 2 passed**, exit 1.\n- With this repair: **3 passed**, exit 0.\n- Python 3.11.2; CPU Future tests only. No GPU/model accuracy run; model arithmetic is unchanged.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot a performance change; no throughput or latency claim. The healthy path still resolves the same Futures, and the failure path now honors the existing full-layer barrier.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changed files pass Ruff 0.15.1 and isort 7.0.0.\n- [x] Extend the existing unit coverage rather than adding a new test file.\n- [x] No user-facing API/configuration change; existing completion contract is preserved.\n- [ ] GPU/model accuracy and speed benchmarks (not run; CPU completion counter only).\n- [x] Keep the repair within the existing counter owner.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39516813744](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39516813744)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39516813669](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39516813669)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39516813395](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39516813395)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
